      },
      "note": [
        "The adjustment is the part of the population increase that cannot be explained by a birth surplus or immigration surplus. It includes births, deaths and occurences of immigration and emigration that were reported during the year, but that occured before 1 January.",
        "For February to December, the population increase is the sum of the birth surplus and the immigration surplus during the month.\r\nFor January, the population increase is the sum of birth surplus and immigration surplus in January and unknown month plus the adjustment.",
        "Marriages and divorces is not disaggregated by gender.",
        "This table is no longer updated."
